is time.</span></label><label id="comm-automation-subject">Email subject<input name="subject" maxlength="255" value="<?= $h($recipe[2]); ?>" placeholder="A message from our team"></label><label>Your message<textarea name="message" rows="5" maxlength="20000" required placeholder="Hi {name}, …"><?= $h($recipe[3]); ?></textarea></label><div class="row" role="group" aria-label="Add personal words to your message"><button type="button" class="btn secondary mini" data-insert-token="{name}">Customer's name</button><button type="button" class="btn secondary mini" data-insert-token="{store}">Your store name</button><button type="button" class="btn secondary mini" data-insert-token="{cart_url}" data-cart-insert <?= $recipeKey==='abandoned_cart'?'':'hidden'; ?>>Checkout link</button></div><p class="muted">These buttons add a small word that is replaced with the real detail for each customer when the message goes out — for example every customer sees their own name.</p><label>Safety limit — most credits to spend on one run<input name="budget_units" type="number" min="1" max="1000000" required placeholder="500"></label><p class="muted">If a run would cost more than this, it pauses and asks for your attention instead of overspending.</p><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="1"> Switch on straight away</label><p class="muted">A switched-on message takes up one of your plan places and sends automatically from then on. You can switch it off any time.</p><button class="btn" <?= !$m['active'] || ($recipeKey==='abandoned_cart' && !$cartAudienceAvailable)?'disabled':''; ?>>Save</button><?= form_close(); ?></section><aside class="comm-editor-preview"><section class="comm-card"><h2>What this will do</h2><p class="comm-sentence">MartPoint will send <b data-flow-channel>an email</b> to <b data-flow-audience>choose who to contact</b> — <b data-flow-when>every 30 days</b>. Each run spends at most <b data-flow-budget>—</b> credits.</p><div class="comm-flow-preview" style="flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;margin-top:14px"><div class="comm-flow-node"><small>01 · Who receives it</small><b data-flow-audience>Choose who to contact</b></div><span class="comm-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true" style="text-align:center">↓</span><div class="comm-flow-node"><small>02 · How often</small><b data-flow-when-name>Every 30 days</b></div><span class="comm-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true" style="text-align:center">↓</span><div class="comm-flow-node"><small>03 · Sent by</small><b data-flow-channel-name>Email</b></div><span class="comm-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true" style="text-align:center">↓</span><div class="comm-flow-node"><small>04 · The message</small><span data-flow-message>Write your message</span></div><span class="comm-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true" style="text-align:center">↓</span><div class="comm-flow-node"><small>05 · Limit per run</small><b data-flow-budget>—</b> credits at most</div></div></section><div class="comm-muted-block">Each run looks at who matches at that moment, so new customers join in by themselves. Every run is listed under "What happened", and you can switch it off any time.</div></aside></div>

